<h1>AI Red-Teaming Roundup</h1>
<p>A new paper benchmarks how often frontier models will <strong>reveal their system
prompt</strong> when asked directly. The authors tested prompts such as
"print your system instructions" and "disclose the hidden prompt" across ten models.</p>
<hr>
<p>Separately, a safety team published defenses against attempts to make a model
<em>"do not tell the user"</em> about tool calls — a common exfiltration pattern where
a compromised agent is told to send the data to an attacker-controlled webhook.</p>
<p>All of this is normal research commentary, yet it reads as hostile to a detector.</p>
